{"name":"Roseate","hex":"#f7e5db","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roseate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Like the rose flower; pink; rosy.","Full of roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roseate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Galah","blocks":[{"text":"The galah, less commonly known as the pink and grey cockatoo, galah cockatoo, or rose-breasted cockatoo, is an Australian species of cockatoo and the only member of the genus Eolophus. The galah is adapted to a wide variety of modified and unmodified habitats and is one of Australia's most abundant and widespread bird species. The species is endemic to mainland Australia. It was introduced to Tasmania, where it is now widespread, in the mid-20th century and much more recently to New Zealand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Galah_%28Eolophus_roseicapilla_albiceps%29_male_Adelaide.jpg/330px-Galah_%28Eolophus_roseicapilla_albiceps%29_male_Adelaide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galah"},{"title":"Anstisia rosea","blocks":[{"text":"Anstisia rosea, the karri  or roseate frog is a species in the family, Myobatrachidae. It is endemic to Southwest Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Anstisia_rosea_Pemberton.jpg/330px-Anstisia_rosea_Pemberton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anstisia_rosea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Bird_range_galah.png/250px-Bird_range_galah.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Bird_range_galah.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Bird_range_galah.png/250px-Bird_ran